{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 9a39f78697cbaa143f8a73088fdd090805d8a5f2. The change is small, and its reasoning is stated at its true strength: **this is a likely cause and not a proven one.** No desktop AI app has rendered this code, and only the next session decides.\n\n**The change.** A resource declares `_meta.ui.domain` only when its package declares one, and no package does. `sandboxDomain` no longer derives a label from the digest. `generation` keeps its value, because it already hashed `domain: null` (`resources.ts:43`). I searched `packages`, `apps` and `docs` for other uses: the only caller of `sandboxDomain` is `resources.ts`. The `inguz.space` screen hosts in `apps/sandbox` and the wrangler files use their own configured origins, so they do not depend on this label. The design note's edit says that correctly.\n\n**The reasoning.** It is right to act on this. The value we sent was not in the form that the host's page requires, by your quotation, and the prototypes that rendered sent none. It is also right to say why this may not be the cause: the person saw different words from the two errors that the page names, and no log gives a reason. I did not read the host's page, so that part rests on your quotation. The two log files in the evidence show the order you state: `resources/read` and no `tools/call` on 1 November, and `resources/read` then `tools/call` on 18 October.\n\n**The fallback.** The table of remaining differences, with the developer tools in the person's steps, is the right plan, because a second failed session otherwise costs the person's time again with no reason named. Please make sure that those steps ask the person to copy the error text from the card's frame.\n\n**Security.** A digest-derived origin would have given each presentation its own origin on a host that honoured it. With no domain, a resource takes the host's default sandbox origin. So isolation between cards on that host is whatever the host gives by default. By your quotation, the old value was out of the form this host accepts, so this gives up no isolation that the host was granting. It adds no authority. If a hosted view later needs a stable origin for its own OAuth, your note says what that head must change. Other hosts have not been checked, so a later host with a different rule needs its own look.\n\n**Architecture.** The field stays optional and package-owned, and a host-specific format is not assumed. No route changes.\n\n**Simplification.** This removes the digest-to-label path, which nothing else used.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` is feebd81b…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 4c2fedf3, exit 0, with 3535 and 1013 tests. Both controls report `DISTINGUISHES`. The browser script passes 24 of 24 by your run, with a loopback host standing in for the app. The merge of main touches no file of this head, so no new gate is owed. I ran `view-resources.test.ts` (5 passed), `security-entry-points` (10 pass), check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (1001, 0 broken) and check-commit-messages (3, 0 flagged) on the merged tree. The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the browser script or the controls.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0514d00eb254317d40a05912139aecf301ff6230","binding":"assigned","head":"9a39f78697cbaa143f8a73088fdd090805d8a5f2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5e0b57b5bb2171774c98bb5c8b40f18b3c3caadb\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:288bffdcb4f448d4c0ecc5e6df5b802aa47a00cd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:29e3b5eaaab87e815403ddc1b6c5529d2541b975","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}